      walkthrough = "**Status: Incomplete**\n\nQuest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Shar Vahl, Divided [zone=1310]\n**Who:**\n- Dar Khura Hamat - NoS [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 120\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 24:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Bloodied Grimling Blade [item=145150]\n- Embroidered Medicine Bag [item=144285]\n- Rough Forensic Kit [item=145149]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Pathmaster Shainai [ _Quests_]\n- Pit Guard Abdar [npc=58141]\n- a dead recruit [npc=57917]\n- a grimling assailant [npc=59807]\n- a grimling attacker [npc=57919]\n- a grimling gatherer [npc=57920]\n- a grimling hunter [npc=57921]\n- a grimling invader [npc=57922]\n- a grimling prisoner [npc=57923]\n- a grimling scout [npc=57924]\n- a grimling skeleton [npc=57925]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Shar Vahl, Divided (10 Points) [quest=12237]\n**Era:** | !Night of Shadows\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sun Oct 23 14:17:15 2022\nModified: Thu Feb 15 05:05:17 2024 | | **Night of Shadows Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\nThis is the 1st Partisan that must be done in order\nPartisan path: Just a Delivery (Group) - A Little Goodwill(Group) - A Peace Offering(Solo)\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this shared task from Dar Khura Hamat in Shar Vahl in the Nights of Shadow expansion. He is located on the roof of the building on the 2nd floor located at -224, -395, -167. He is also on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Dar Khura Hamat'\nDar Khura Hamat says, 'Ah, an adventurer. Hail and well met!' With a friendly smile, he pats Gidono on the arm in welcome. The Dar Khura takes pause and his gaze becomes one of discernment. 'You... you wouldn't happen to be [looking for work], would you?'\nYou say, 'I would, actually. I'm looking for work.'\nDar Khura Hamat sighs in relief. 'Then do I have the job for you, friend. It's really a basic one, a simple [delivery]. I would do it myself, but I can't really leave the shop at the moment.'\nYou say, 'I can do a delivery.'\nDar Khura Hamat says, 'You know, you're a life-saver. The delivery's down in the Pit, so I do have to warn you that the trek is a little dangerous. You have a lot of experience in the field, yeah? You should be fine. Let me know when you're ready for the [herbs].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Just a Delivery'.\nYou say, 'I'm ready for the herbs.'\nDar Khura Hamat says, 'Take these herbs over to Pit Guard Abdar, and he'll organize your payment from there. You've got this.'\nYou are given: Embroidered Medicine Bag\n\n---\n\nThings are not right in Shar Vahl. At least you have a nice quick job to do that should get you a little coin while in town.\n1\\. Take the Embroidered Medicine Bag to Pit Guard Abdar 0/1 Shard Vahl, Divided\nPit Guard Abdar can be found at in the pit around Shar Vahl in the Southeast at /waypoint -787, -780, -294 on top of a boulder.\nP 787.5539, 780.7523, -294.2293, 0, 0, 0, 3, Pit\\_Guard\\_Abdar\nUpon Handin:\nYou say, 'Hail, Pit Guard Abdar'\nPit Guard Abdar says, 'Well met, friend. May I be of assistance?'\nYou offered 1 Embroidered Medicine Bag to Pit Guard Abdar.\nPit Guard Abdar examines the crest on the medicine bag and smirks. 'Well.' He gives the bag a gentle pat and places it in a larger satchel at his post. He isn't handling the agreed-upon [pay].\nYou complete the trade with Pit Guard Abdar.\nYour task 'Just a Delivery' has been updated.\n2\\. Discuss payment with Pit Guard Abdar 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nYou say, 'What about my pay for the delivery?'\nPit Guard Abdar says, 'Did Hamat promise you pay? Well, that's so kind of him, isn't it?' The Guard's fur is bristled and his expression is on-edge. 'You're an [outsider], a Norrathian. This doesn't concern you.'\nYour task 'Just a Delivery' has been updated.\nYou say, 'Outsider? What is this about?'\nPit Guard Abdar says, 'There's things better left to the locals. [Move along].'\nYou say, 'No, I'm not going to move along. Again, what is this about?'\nPit Guard Abdar says, 'Persistent, aren't you? If this isn't about the pay, go kill eight grimlings down here and report back. We, the Pit guards, will watch. Just do your thing and \"adventure\" and we'll see where we go from there. Good? Good.'\n3\\. Kill 8 grimlings within the Shar Vahl Pit 0/8 Shar Vahl, Divided\n> **Quest Text:** Things would have been better if you simply got paid for the delivery job, but Pit Guard Abdar has requested some slaughtering of grimlings in the meantime. Maybe some information as to what is going on will some with payment.\n4\\. Check in with Pit Guard Abdar 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nYou say, 'Hail, Pit Guard Abdar'\nPit Guard Abdar gives a long, drawn-out sigh and scratches the fur at his jawline. 'You have skills, I'll give you that.' He turns his gaze out towards the Pit again. 'What do you know about the current state of [Shar Vahl]?'\nYour task 'Just a Delivery' has been updated.\nYou say, 'Some people have commented that Shar Vahl is unsafe lately.'\nPit Guard Abdar says, '\"Unsafe\" is a simplification, but it works in terms of basic understanding. I know it's none of your business, but would you care to [help] us in tracking down just how things have gone down how they have?'\nYou say, 'Yes, I can help.'\nPit Guard Abdar says, 'Hamat has himself a good judge of character then. Welcome to the team, I guess. Here, take this letter to Pathmaster Shainai. She'll be able to direct you further. He takes a pause, looking up at the sky. 'Based on the time of day, you'll be able to find her in the domicile above Melek's tavern.'\nWARNING TASK LOCKS Next Stage\nWARNING TASK LOCKS Next Stage\nWARNING TASK LOCKS Next Stage\n5\\. Take Abdar's Letter to Pathmaster Shainai 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nYou offered 1 Abdar's Letter to Pathmaster Shainai.\nPathmaster Shainai says, 'Oh, good day!' Her cheerful expression turns curious and she inquires, 'What is this?' She looks at the wax seal holding the flap of the envelope closed. Peeling it off, she crushes the wax between her fingers, obscuring the image pressed upon it, then digs out the letter, scanning it with a serious set to her jaw. 'Thanks for offering to help. Welcome to the [cause], Thorque.'\nYou complete the trade with Pathmaster Shainai.\nYour task 'Just a Delivery' has been updated.\n6\\. Get further instructions from Pathmaster Shainai 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nYou say, 'What can I do for the cause?'\nPathmaster Shainai says, 'As someone who has spent their time adventuring, you're more likely to be seen without an alignment - at least to start. Let's see if we can use that to our advantage. It's said that there's a recruit who lost their life in the Pit, and we need to prove that it wasn't the Sahtebi adherents who did it to them. Can you find their [body], and examine the area around it for signs of the assailant?'\nYour task 'Just a Delivery' has been updated.\nYou say, 'I can look for the body.'\nPathmaster Shainai says, 'Thank you so much. Here's a forensics kit. Once we have a definitive confirmation it wasn't another Vah Shir, we should have more freedom to remove them and bring them back to their family. Everyone has been afraid to help in this case as they didn't want to anger one of the largest spiritual factions in the city. This should put a lot of concerns to rest.'\nYou are given a Rough Forensic Kit.\n7\\. Find the body of the recruit and examine the area with the Rough Forensic Kit 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nThe body of \"a dead recruit\" is on the northwest side of the pit, where there is a big angle in the wall on the map.\n/way 777, 953, -326\nClick the Rough Forensic Kit near the body and 3 mobs will spawn and attack.\n8\\. Kill the 3 grimlings lying in wait 0/3 Shar Vahl, Divided\n3x a grimling assailant spawn, kill them.\n9\\. Loot a Bloodied Grimling Blade 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nThis will be on the a grimling assailant's corpse\n10\\. Take the Bloodied Grimling Blade back to Pathmaster Shainai 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nGive 1 Bloodied Grimling Blade to Pathmaster Shainai.\nYou offered 1 Bloodied Grimling Blade to Pathmaster Shainai.\nPathmaster Shainai carefully takes the weapon and gives the viscous blood a few deep sniffs. 'That's definitely Vah Shir blood. It may be premature, but this may be the weapon itself and priceless to our cause.'\nYour task 'Just a Delivery' has been updated.\n11\\. Take the Rough Forensic Kit back to Pathmaster Shainai 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nGive 1 Rough Forensic Kit to Pathmaster Shainai.\nYou offered 1 Rough Forensic Kit to Pathmaster Shainai.\nPathmaster Shainai says, 'Thanks. It seems to have served us well.'\nYour task 'Just a Delivery' has been updated.\nYou have received a replay timer for 'Just a Delivery': 0d:0h:30m remaining.\nPathmaster Shainai is fairly confident that the weapon found is the weapon that killed the recruit. At least that's one mystery solved.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n177 plat 8 silver 4 copper\nExperience\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
